course: dictionary
lesson: 11117
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. White is a good example: it can be a colour, the name of a part of an egg, or a way to describe a pale face. Look at the words around it to find the meaning that fits.
explain: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» Here white means a colour. Try the colour meaning in the sentence and it still makes sense.
explain: Words also change their job in a sentence. White can describe a thing, as in «white as snow», or it can name a part, as in «the whites of your eyes». Ask yourself: is this word describing something, or naming something?
fact: White is the colour of snow and milk.
fact: The white of an egg is the clear part that turns white when cooked.
fact: The whites of your eyes are the white parts around the coloured part.
fact: White light is made of all the colours of the rainbow.
fact: «Stars have different colours: the hottest are blue-white, our Sun is yellow-white.»
exercise: In «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears», what does white mean? | A type of food | A kind of animal | *A colour | A loud noise
exercise: What is the white of an egg? | *The clear part that turns white when cooked | A small bird | A hard shell | The yellow middle
exercise: Which sentence uses white as a noun, naming a part? | «White snow fell all night.» | *«She could see the whites of his eyes.» | «The walls were white.» | «White bread is soft.»
test: A box has 12 counters, and 5 of them are white. How many are not white? | *7 | 5 | 17 | 12
test: What is white light made of? | Only black | Just one colour | *All the colours of the rainbow | Snow
exam: Which of these is a true meaning of white? | Black | A kind of rain | *The colour of snow and milk | A loud noise
